\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Vertex and boundary generators}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [cellular anti-reflection](fdip-00XQ) acts on every
paired generator by
##{\begin{aligned}
 \Theta\psi_{v_j}&=\bar\psi_{v_{1-j}},&
 \Theta\bar\psi_{v_j}&=\psi_{v_{1-j}},\\
 \Theta\psi_{e_j}&=-u_j\bar\psi_{e_j},&
 \Theta\bar\psi_{e_j}&=-u_j\psi_{e_j}
 \qquad(j=0,1).
\end{aligned}}
The strict positive half has basis
#{1,\psi_{v_1},\bar\psi_{v_1},b_1}, where
#{b_j=\bar\psi_{v_j}\psi_{v_j}}.
Its even subalgebra is spanned by #{1,b_1}.
Each #{b_j} is invariant under the local sign gauge action,
and order reversal gives #{\Theta b_1=b_0}.}

\p{Both edges are reflection-boundary cells. Their generators
are integrated in #{\ell}, even though neither edge is in
an open half. Exchanging their barred and unbarred labels
does not move those geometric cells off the boundary.}
